Z||000000||sluppy123||06-24-99||09:47 PM||||I currently own two Fiero's-87' GT & 85' sc.<br>I'm having big troubles with the 85. It has a  problem, just about every time I step on the gas it stumbles and back-fires. It only does it when the engine is in gear and warm.(4-cylinder,auto) The engine has not set any trouble codes. I've checked the timing and it was spot on 8 degrees. The engine only has 20k miles on it so i don't think it's engine related.I've replaced the plugs, wires, distributor cap and rotor, fuel filter, etc...<p>If anybody has any suggestions please help.
Z||000001||theogre||06-24-99||10:14 PM||||hook it up to an ECM scanner. (The AutoXray GM scanner is about 150$us, and works wit both cars.) A scanner, Not a code reader! the scanner can actually monitor a sensor, the code reader only reads error codes.<p>I suspect one of 2 sensors could be scragged. MAP, or TPS. for the giggles check the ECM for codes. you could have one and not have seen the light go on.<p>The MAP sensor reads maifold vac, and at it's result is used to calculate Timing advance like the old Vac advance on a traditional motor. ((I.E a carb with a mechanical distibutor.))<p>The TPS(Throttle Position Sensor) may be worn out, it's a mechanical part that wears, and as a result it is not getting a good pedal reading to the ECM.
Z||000002||theogre||06-24-99||10:17 PM||||hook it up to an ECM scanner. (The AutoXray GM scanner is about 150$us, and works wit both cars.) A scanner, Not a code reader! the scanner can actually monitor a sensor, the code reader only reads error codes.<p>I suspect one of 2 sensors could be scragged. MAP, or TPS. for the giggles check the ECM for codes. you could have one and not have seen the light go on.<p>The MAP sensor reads maifold vac, and at it's result is used to calculate Timing advance like the old Vac advance on a traditional motor. ((I.E a carb with a mechanical distibutor.))<p>The TPS(Throttle Position Sensor) may be worn out, it's a mechanical part that wears, and as a result it is not getting a good pedal reading to the ECM.
